# Patch:        010-exposed-ops-and-layout
# Phase:        post
# Target:       extraction/P3BinaryDft/Extraction/Funs.lean
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        reshape
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 22 (Aeneas's saturating operations
#               have no exposed body).
# Cost:         the exposed model of `saturating_sub` on usize in HaxExt.lean,
#               trusted as the rest of HaxExt is.
# Upstreamable: yes: aeneas can mark its saturating operations `@[expose]`,
#               and pass the type argument of `size_of`.
# Drop when:    aeneas exposes them and emits `size_of`'s type argument.
#
# The two saturating calls go to HaxExt's exposed model, so a proof can state what they return.
#
# One is the height of the step table, the other the tile height of the schedule.
#
# aeneas emits `size_of` without its type argument, which Lean cannot infer.
#
# The call passes the element type, which is in scope.
#
--- a/extraction/P3BinaryDft/Extraction/Funs.lean
